## Repro (already in the tree)
`ZLINK_TEST_CASE=test_router_handover_tcp core/build-dev/bin/test_router_reject_disconnected_without_app_recv` — second ROUTER (same RID, tcp) is
CONNECTED but the binder never publishes READY; `asio_zmp_engine.cpp:644` looks up the accepted pair by peer RID, `socket_base_api.cpp:86-89` returns the
existing pair id for count-two, and `socket_base_api.cpp:336-339` (post-patch numbering) treats the new pipe as another pipe on an occupied lane and
terminates the new pipe and the old pair's application/completion pipes — before `router_admission.cpp` HANDOVER/REJECT runs. Pre-existing (also on
baseline) per the D-092 report.

## What to do
1. Root cause: which owner decides the pair identity of an accepted connection whose peer RID already has a pair — the transport engine (physical
   connection = new pair, D-086) or the socket lane table? Per spec the physical pair identity is per connection; RID duplicate policy is the ROUTER's
   admission decision. Make the accepted connection get its own pair and reach admission, where HANDOVER takes over (old pipe → standby per D-B96) and
   REJECT closes the duplicate (D-088). One owner for "which pair does this pipe belong to"; remove the count-two reuse special case if that is the
   duplicate rule. State rule count before/after.
2. Regression coverage: the existing new test's `test_router_handover_tcp` + REJECT tcp case must now exercise real admission (assert the binder READY
   and, for HANDOVER, that the old pipe is standby and the request contract of D-090 holds; for REJECT, DISCONNECTED without app recv per D-092).
   Add a case for same-RID tcp reconnect with a *different* endpoint identity (client reconnects after network drop) — HANDOVER must take over.
3. Gate: new test `--repeat until-fail:10` (all cases), targeted `test_router_reject_duplicate|test_socket_disconnect_boundary|test_router_reciprocal_handover_lanes|
   test_ctx_term_fixed_rid_handover|test_router_handover|test_transport_matrix|test_monitor_connection_identity|test_multi_socket_contract_regressions`, full
   ctest once (expect only hotpath n/a).
4. Deliverable in the MAIN tree: `doc/plan/c016-worklog/core-tcp-router-same-rid-handover-pair-summary.md` (cause file:line, fix, owner / spec clause /
